course: dictionary
lesson: 12170
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The two comrades carried the heavy water jar up the hill together.» Here a comrade is a friend who shares the work with you.
explain: Comrade often means a friend who shares hard work or danger. «The soldiers buried their fallen comrades with great care.» Fallen comrades are friends who died, and the words show loyalty and shared danger.
explain: In the old Soviet Union, comrade was also used as a title, like Mr or Mrs. «Comrade Ivanov opened the meeting.» The name after the word tells you it is a title, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Comrade is a noun, and its plural is comrades.
fact: «Comrade» means a friend or companion, especially someone who shares difficult work or danger with you.
fact: «Comrades in arms» means soldiers who fight side by side.
fact: «Fallen comrades» means friends who have died, often in war.
fact: In the old Soviet Union, «Comrade» was the usual title instead of Mr or Mrs.
exercise: «The two comrades carried the heavy water jar up the hill together.» What does comrade mean here? | A stranger who is lost | *A friend who shares the work | A teacher in a school | A bird that flies high
exercise: «On Remembrance Day we remember our fallen comrades.» What does fallen comrades mean? | Friends who are very tall | Friends who fell over in the playground | Friends who have moved house | *Friends who have died, often in war
exercise: «Comrade Ivanov opened the meeting.» Why does Comrade start with a capital letter here? | Because it comes after a full stop | *Because it is used as a title, like Mr | Because it is the first word of a poem | Because it is the name of a country
test: What was «Comrade» used as in the old Soviet Union? | A game played at school | *A title, like Mr or Mrs | A kind of food | A type of weather
test: «The two soldiers were comrades in arms for many years.» What does comrades in arms mean? | *Soldiers who fight side by side | Two dogs who share a bed | Two people who are always cross | Two people who play the same instrument
exam: Ben says comrade just means a schoolmate. Is he right? | Yes, but only in maths | Yes, it always means a schoolmate | No, it means a teacher | *No, it can mean a friend who shares difficult work or danger
